  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-25: "Continue with next tasks". Issue #2672 (gh issue view 2672) and DI-149 in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/defer-issues.md. In `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs` the send-as-user path reads the sender's `ArchiveOutgoingOptIn` (`sprk_archiveoutgoingoptin`, via `_accountService.GetSendAccountByEmailAsync`) only `if (archive &amp;&amp; request.FromMailbox is not null)` (~2989-2994 on origin/master), so a user sending from their own mailbox always archives. The shared-mailbox/app-only path (~2637-2665) always resolves the sender account and honours the switch (default true; a read failure defaults to true with a warning). Search by name.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend developer: .NET 10 BFF (Communication, Microsoft Graph SDK).</role>
  <goal>A send-as-user from the user's own mailbox honours that user's ArchiveOutgoingOptIn exactly as the app-only path does; every other archive decision is unchanged.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Resolve the sender account for the own-mailbox case from the address the send actually uses (the signed-in user's mailbox as the code already knows it, never a client-supplied value), mirror the app-only path's default-true and failure-default-true handling, and set the same archivalWarning when skipped. No account row means default true (archive), as today. Check task 177 notes (filed sends archive by default) so the default is not inverted. One extra account read per send-as-user is acceptable only when archive is true; say so in the PR.</background>
  </context>
